    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen a file is reloaded `autoread` there is no reliable way to access the contents of the buffer *before* the reload happens.\n\n- `FileChangedShell` fires only if `autoread` is false\n- when `BufReadPre` fires the buffer content is empty\n- `BufUnload` fires when reloading the buffer manually using `:edit` but not when the reload is triggered by `autoread`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nEither one of the existing autocmds should be adjusted, or a new one should be created specifically for this use case.\n\nIt seems like `FileChangedShell` could be triggered also when `autoread` is on but it might be a breaking change.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "An event probably will be helpful, but I think also a more formalized way to get the \"current buffer bytes\" (and optionally a hash thereof) is needed:\n\n\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/8648\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/39348\n\n\nSomewhat related, currently `:lockmarks edit` doesn't do anything useful. Would be nice if a file could be reloaded without clobbering those marks. However it doesn't really solve the larger request here.",
